  "title": "NETBCI2026: NETBCI: longitudinal right-hand motor imagery vs rest BCI training",
  "description": "A longitudinal EEG dataset of right-hand motor imagery versus rest during brain-computer interface (BCI) training. Nineteen healthy participants completed four sessions on four separate days, with six online feedback runs per session. Each trial used a one-dimensional two-target cursor task, with visual feedback driven by sustained right-hand grasping imagery or rest. The data were recorded with a 74-channel EEG system and are distributed in BIDS format with HED annotations.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 250 Hz with a 74-channel Easycap passive Ag/AgCl cap, amplified by a MEGIN TRIUX system and referenced to the mastoids. Stimulus presentation and online feedback were run with BCI2000. Each trial had a 1 s inter-stimulus interval followed by a 5 s target presentation, with cursor feedback from 3 to 6 s. The protocol specified 32 trials per run.",
